hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1750","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate: ""O Allah! I seek refuge in You from miserliness, laziness, the worst age, the punishment of the grave, the trial of Dajjal, and from the trials of life and death (that You protect me from them)."
